# Vultr's settings (`metacomputer vm create NAME --on vultr` writes them to config/vms/NAME.env), as comments:
# nothing here is read as a setting; config/defaults.env has the defaults every computer shares. Its docs: docs/remote.md, Hetzner Cloud, DigitalOcean and Vultr.
#   PLACE=vultr, PROVIDER=vultr, TRANSPORT=ssh
#   SIZE                     vc2-2c-4gb (the default), vc2-4c-8gb
#   REGION                   ewr (the default), ord, dfw, sea, lax, atl, ams, lhr
#   IDLE_STOP                off by default (it would save nothing, and Vultr doesn't see a guest power itself off)
#   EGRESS                   internet or off: its own firewall only (Vultr's firewall filters only what comes in)
# Its credentials, only from the environment of the command that needs them (never a file):
#   VULTR_API_KEY            an API key (with the access control list allowing this Mac's address)
